       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That's 5 times the usual maximum outpatient and inpatient dose of 3,200 mg/day, and it could cause serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm.\n\nWas a different dose intended? Typical oral adult regimens are:\n- **400 mg every 6 hours (four times daily)**, which is 1,600 mg/day, for mild to moderate pain or fever.\n- **600 mg four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum, usually for inflammatory conditions.\n\nPlease confirm the dose, for example \"400 mg PO QID\", and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 4000 mg per dose, tell me the clinical reason and I'll go from there. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
